WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:03.927
KATARA: Water...

00:04.844 --> 00:06.137
Earth...

00:06.721 --> 00:08.640
Fire...

00:08.848 --> 00:10.183
Air.

00:11.351 --> 00:12.852
Long ago...

00:12.936 --> 00:14.687
The four nations lived together
in harmony.

00:14.771 --> 00:19.317
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.901 --> 00:23.780
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements could stop them.

00:23.905 --> 00:25.448
But when the world needed him most

00:25.532 --> 00:27.617
he vanished.

00:27.700 --> 00:31.246
100 years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

00:31.329 --> 00:32.872
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.206 --> 00:35.250
And although his airbending
skills were great

00:35.583 --> 00:37.794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.877 --> 00:39.003
AANG: Oof.

00:39.087 --> 00:43.091
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:43.758 --> 00:45.510
( ♪... )

00:48.012 --> 00:50.473
( MAN READING )

00:50.765 --> 00:52.684
OZAI: I am proud of you, Prince Zuko.

00:52.892 --> 00:55.812
You slayed the Avatar.

00:57.021 --> 00:59.566
ZUKO: You're so beautiful
when you hate the world.

00:59.899 --> 01:01.734
I don't hate you.

01:01.818 --> 01:03.027
I don't hate you, too.

01:05.196 --> 01:07.657
I have everything I always wanted.

01:07.740 --> 01:09.617
But it's not at all
how I thought it would be.

01:09.701 --> 01:12.287
The Avatar is alive.

01:12.453 --> 01:13.580
I want you to find him...

01:13.955 --> 01:15.832
...And end him.

01:17.959 --> 01:21.629
( ♪... )

01:23.715 --> 01:25.758
( GROWLS )

01:25.967 --> 01:29.053
TY LEE: I'm so excited to spend
the weekend on Ember Island.

01:29.304 --> 01:32.265
It's gonna be great to hang out
on the beach and do nothing.

01:32.807 --> 01:34.475
Doing nothing is a waste of time.

01:34.559 --> 01:36.477
We're being sent away on
a forced vacation.

01:36.561 --> 01:37.645
I feel like a child.

01:37.729 --> 01:39.272
Lighten up.

01:39.355 --> 01:40.815
So dad wants to meet
with his advisors alone

01:40.898 --> 01:42.358
without anyone else around.

01:42.442 --> 01:44.110
Don't take it personally.

01:44.319 --> 01:47.155
Doesn't your family have
a house on Ember Island?

01:47.572 --> 01:49.449
We used to come every
summer when we were kids.

01:49.616 --> 01:51.034
That must've been fun.

01:51.451 --> 01:53.870
That was a long time ago.

02:05.381 --> 02:08.551
BOTH: Welcome to Ember Island, kids.

02:20.605 --> 02:22.565
It smells like old lady in here.

02:22.649 --> 02:23.900
Gee, I wonder why.

02:25.735 --> 02:27.695
TY LEE: Who are these two beautiful women?

02:27.904 --> 02:29.864
Can't you tell?

02:29.947 --> 02:31.699
- It's Li and me.
- It's Lo and me.

02:31.824 --> 02:33.284
( RETCHES )

02:33.618 --> 02:36.829
Ooh, I love this seashell bedspread.

02:36.913 --> 02:38.498
Are you serious?

02:38.581 --> 02:40.333
It looks like the beach
threw up all over it.

02:40.792 --> 02:42.919
LI: We know you're upset

02:43.002 --> 02:45.755
that you were forced
to come here this weekend.

02:45.838 --> 02:48.591
But Ember Island is a magical place.

02:49.217 --> 02:50.968
Keep an open mind.

02:51.052 --> 02:53.054
Give it a chance.

02:53.388 --> 02:56.474
And it can help you understand
yourselves and each other.

02:58.267 --> 03:01.020
The beach has a special way

03:01.104 --> 03:03.314
of smoothing even the most ragged edges.

03:04.273 --> 03:06.401
( YAWNS )

03:06.984 --> 03:09.487
BOTH: Time to hit the beach.

03:12.824 --> 03:14.826
TOPH: Aang, I know swimming is fun and all

03:14.909 --> 03:17.954
but do you really think you should be
exposing yourself like that?

03:18.079 --> 03:19.080
Cover up.

03:19.247 --> 03:21.290
What?
I'm wearing trunks.

03:21.499 --> 03:23.584
I know, it's your tattoos
I'm worried about.

03:23.668 --> 03:25.253
What if someone sees you?

03:25.336 --> 03:26.587
There are walls all around us.

03:26.671 --> 03:27.880
It's completely safe.

03:29.048 --> 03:31.008
( CHIRPS )

03:32.927 --> 03:33.970
AANG: Whoo, hey!

03:34.053 --> 03:36.889
( MOMO CHIRPS )

03:37.098 --> 03:40.727
( LAUGHING )

03:42.019 --> 03:45.606
This has got to be the most
boring job in the Fire Nation.

03:45.815 --> 03:47.734
- Nothing ever happens.
-( SNIFFS )

03:47.817 --> 03:49.944
AANG: Whoa!

03:53.239 --> 03:54.866
Let's go again.

04:00.371 --> 04:02.123
The Avatar's alive.

04:02.206 --> 04:04.292
We better send a messenger hawk
to the Fire Lord.

04:07.086 --> 04:08.087
( HAWK CRIES )

04:11.799 --> 04:13.217
A black ribbon message.

04:13.760 --> 04:15.720
This is so exciting.

04:15.803 --> 04:16.804
( LAUGHS )

04:34.781 --> 04:36.199
CHILDREN: Ahh!

04:37.241 --> 04:39.535
Hey, you need some help unpacking?

04:39.619 --> 04:42.121
- Sure, thanks.
-( GRUNTS )

04:52.715 --> 04:56.260
Could you scooch just
a little bit more to the...

04:56.803 --> 04:58.596
Perfect.

04:58.721 --> 05:00.473
( CHILD LAUGHS )

05:01.599 --> 05:02.683
Here...

05:02.767 --> 05:04.227
This is for you.

05:04.310 --> 05:06.187
Why would I want that?

05:06.270 --> 05:07.814
I saw it and I thought it was pretty.

05:08.022 --> 05:09.398
Don't girls like stuff like this?

05:09.607 --> 05:11.859
( SCOFFS ) Maybe stupid girls.

05:12.527 --> 05:13.528
Forget it!

05:23.246 --> 05:24.789
Wow, thanks.

05:24.872 --> 05:26.499
This is so pretty.

05:26.582 --> 05:28.167
Not as pretty as you are.

05:28.251 --> 05:30.127
That shell's not so great.

05:30.795 --> 05:32.755
Ahem, shade... Shade.

05:35.842 --> 05:38.052
I thought since it's so hot... Here.

05:39.929 --> 05:41.180
Thanks.

05:41.389 --> 05:43.307
This is really refreshing.

05:49.355 --> 05:51.232
Hey, beach bums, we're playing next.

05:51.315 --> 05:53.484
Ty lee, get over here now.

06:01.075 --> 06:04.370
( GIGGLING )

06:08.749 --> 06:10.793
See that girl with the silly pigtails?

06:11.002 --> 06:13.254
When she runs towards the ball

06:13.504 --> 06:15.214
there's just the slightest
hesitation of her left foot.

06:15.298 --> 06:17.592
I'm willing to bet a childhood
injury has weakened her.

06:17.675 --> 06:20.094
Keep serving the ball to her
left and we'll destroy her

06:20.177 --> 06:21.846
and the rest of her team.

06:22.096 --> 06:23.931
Dismissed.

06:53.169 --> 06:55.463
( FIRE CRACKLING )

06:55.671 --> 06:58.799
Yes, we defeated you for all time.

06:59.008 --> 07:02.094
You will never rise from the ashes of your
shame and humiliation.

07:03.262 --> 07:05.598
Well, that was fun.

07:05.681 --> 07:07.350
I'm having a party tonight.

07:07.558 --> 07:08.559
You should come by.

07:08.768 --> 07:09.769
Sure...

07:09.936 --> 07:11.062
I love parties.

07:11.395 --> 07:12.688
Your friend can come, too.

07:12.772 --> 07:15.399
Uh, what about me and my brother?

07:15.608 --> 07:17.193
Aren't you going to invite us?

07:17.526 --> 07:20.237
You don't know who we are, do you?

07:20.321 --> 07:22.239
Don't you know who we are?

07:22.448 --> 07:24.241
We're Chan and Ruon-Jian.

07:24.450 --> 07:25.451
Yeah.

07:27.578 --> 07:29.372
But fine, you're invited.

07:29.455 --> 07:31.415
Just so you know, though

07:31.624 --> 07:33.125
some of the most important teenagers in
the Fire Nation

07:33.334 --> 07:34.961
are gonna be at this party so...

07:35.169 --> 07:36.212
Try and act normal.

07:36.420 --> 07:37.713
We'll do our best.

07:44.178 --> 07:46.138
ZUKO: Why didn't you tell
those guys who we were?

07:46.222 --> 07:47.348
AZULA: I guess I was intrigued.

07:47.682 --> 07:49.600
I'm so used to people worshipping us.

07:49.725 --> 07:51.102
They should.

07:51.185 --> 07:53.145
Yes, I know, and I love it.

07:53.396 --> 07:55.356
But for once, I just wanted to see

07:55.439 --> 07:57.441
how people would treat us if
they didn't know who we were.

07:57.525 --> 07:59.443
Like waves washing away

07:59.527 --> 08:01.904
the footprints on the sand

08:02.154 --> 08:05.908
Ember island gives everyone a clean slate.

08:06.075 --> 08:08.703
Ember Island reveals the true you.

08:11.831 --> 08:13.708
- To the party.
- To the party.

08:13.791 --> 08:15.751
( HAWK CRIES )

08:18.671 --> 08:19.672
( CRYING CONTINUES )

08:22.800 --> 08:24.719
( SQUAWKING )

08:27.888 --> 08:28.889
( HAWK CRIES )

08:31.642 --> 08:34.520
( BIRDS CRYING )

08:58.461 --> 09:00.254
Um... You're a little early.

09:00.463 --> 09:01.547
No one's here yet.

09:01.756 --> 09:03.257
I heard you telling someone

09:03.340 --> 09:04.717
You'd be partying from dusk till dawn.

09:04.925 --> 09:07.219
It's dusk so we're here.

09:07.511 --> 09:10.139
But that's just an expression.

09:10.514 --> 09:12.475
We are the perfect party guests.

09:12.600 --> 09:14.643
We arrive right on time
because we are very punctual.

09:19.732 --> 09:21.233
CHAN: All right, listen,
my dad's an admiral.

09:21.317 --> 09:22.526
He has no idea I'm having this party

09:22.735 --> 09:24.528
so don't mess anything up.

09:26.447 --> 09:30.159
That's a sharp outfit, Chan... Careful.

09:30.284 --> 09:33.746
You could puncture the hull
of an Empire-class Fire Nation battleship

09:33.871 --> 09:36.040
leaving thousands to drown at sea...

09:36.540 --> 09:40.002
Because it's so sharp.

09:40.086 --> 09:43.297
Um... Thanks.

09:49.804 --> 09:52.306
Hey, first ones here, huh?

09:52.389 --> 09:56.018
He thinks he's so great.

09:56.227 --> 09:58.312
Well, what do you think of him?

09:58.521 --> 10:00.147
I don't have any opinion about him.

10:00.231 --> 10:01.816
I hardly know him.

10:01.899 --> 10:03.984
- You like him, don't you?
-( IRRITATED SIGH )

10:10.699 --> 10:12.660
So how do you know Ty Lee?

10:12.868 --> 10:14.912
I met her at the beach today.

10:14.995 --> 10:17.039
She was pretty impressed
by a sand pagoda that I made for her.

10:17.248 --> 10:20.459
Well, I met her first.

10:20.668 --> 10:24.088
Look, it doesn't matter
who I met first 'cause I like you all.

10:24.296 --> 10:26.215
But which one of us do you like?

10:26.423 --> 10:28.175
- Yeah.
- Tell us.

10:28.300 --> 10:30.052
I don't know, I don't know.

10:31.762 --> 10:32.847
( ALL GRUNT )

10:32.930 --> 10:33.931
ALL: Ooh.

10:34.014 --> 10:35.307
Ahh...

10:35.391 --> 10:37.268
Oh, I'm glad you're here.

10:37.351 --> 10:39.353
Those boys won't leave me alone.

10:39.436 --> 10:41.397
I guess they all just like me too much.

10:41.480 --> 10:44.441
Come on, Ty Lee,
you can't be this ignorant.

10:44.650 --> 10:46.527
What are you talking about?

10:46.735 --> 10:49.613
Those boys only like you because
you make it so easy for them.

10:49.822 --> 10:51.782
You're not a challenge-you're a tease.

10:51.991 --> 10:54.326
It's not like they
actually care who you are.

10:54.451 --> 10:56.036
( SOBBING )

10:56.328 --> 10:59.206
OK, OK, calm down.

10:59.415 --> 11:01.083
I didn't mean what I said.

11:01.167 --> 11:04.336
Look, maybe I just said it
because I was a little...

11:04.420 --> 11:05.421
( WHISPERS ) Jealous.

11:05.504 --> 11:07.381
What?

11:07.464 --> 11:09.425
You were jealous of me?

11:09.508 --> 11:13.345
Um, but, you're the most beautiful,
smartest, perfect girl in the world.

11:13.429 --> 11:14.972
Well, you're right about all those things.

11:15.181 --> 11:16.932
But for some reason when I meet boys

11:17.141 --> 11:19.393
they act as if I'm going to do
something horrible to them.

11:19.602 --> 11:22.563
( LAUGHS ) But you probably
would do something horrible to them.

11:22.771 --> 11:26.317
I'm sure they're just intimidated by you.

11:26.525 --> 11:28.569
OK, look, if you want a boy to like you

11:28.777 --> 11:30.571
just look at him and smile a lot

11:30.779 --> 11:33.490
and laugh at everything he says
even if it's not funny.

11:33.574 --> 11:38.037
Well, that sounds
really shallow and stupid.

11:38.245 --> 11:39.246
Let's try it.

11:39.413 --> 11:40.873
OK.

11:41.081 --> 11:42.875
( AS BOY ) "Hey, there, sweet sugar cakes.

11:43.083 --> 11:45.252
"How ya likin' this party?"

11:45.461 --> 11:47.546
( LAUGHS GIDDILY )

11:47.755 --> 11:49.340
( SILENCE )

11:49.548 --> 11:52.426
MAI: I'm bored.
ZUKO: I know.

11:52.509 --> 11:54.887
- I'm hungry.
- So what?

11:55.095 --> 11:56.847
So find me some food.

11:57.056 --> 11:58.057
Sure.

12:01.310 --> 12:03.729
Chan, I'm ready for a tour of the house.

12:07.816 --> 12:10.527
CHAN: Is this your first time
on Ember Island?

12:10.736 --> 12:13.072
AZULA: No, I used to come here years ago.

12:13.280 --> 12:15.658
It's a great place if you like sand.

12:15.866 --> 12:18.369
( LAUGHING )

12:18.452 --> 12:22.373
Yeah, it's like, "Welcome to Sandy Land."

12:22.581 --> 12:24.667
( BOTH LAUGH )

12:27.294 --> 12:30.756
Your arms look so strong.

12:30.965 --> 12:33.300
Yeah, I know.

12:36.804 --> 12:38.389
You're pretty.

12:38.472 --> 12:40.933
( SWEETLY ) Together, you and I will be...

12:41.141 --> 12:43.560
( FIRMLY ) The strongest couple
in the entire world.

12:43.644 --> 12:45.729
We will dominate the earth!

12:49.525 --> 12:51.944
Uh... I gotta go.

13:03.747 --> 13:05.749
Hey, watch it.

13:05.958 --> 13:07.668
That food was for my cranky girlfriend.

13:13.299 --> 13:14.300
Whoa...

13:15.926 --> 13:17.177
What are you doing?

13:17.386 --> 13:18.846
Stop talking to my girlfriend.

13:19.054 --> 13:21.307
Relax, it's just a party.

13:21.765 --> 13:22.766
Uh!

13:23.976 --> 13:26.520
Zuko, what is wrong with you?

13:26.603 --> 13:28.397
What's wrong with me?

13:28.605 --> 13:30.024
Your temper's out of control.

13:30.232 --> 13:32.026
You blow up over every little thing.

13:32.234 --> 13:35.070
You're so impatient and
hot-headed and angry.

13:35.279 --> 13:37.865
Well, at least I feel something...
As opposed to you.

13:38.073 --> 13:39.408
You have no passion for anything.

13:39.616 --> 13:42.161
You're just a big blah.

13:42.369 --> 13:44.538
It's over, Zuko.

13:44.747 --> 13:46.248
We're done.

13:46.457 --> 13:48.625
Who broke my Nana's vase?

13:50.586 --> 13:51.754
That's it, you're out of here.

13:51.962 --> 13:53.589
I was just leaving.

13:53.672 --> 13:56.383
Have fun by yourself, loser boy.

13:56.925 --> 13:58.135
Nice.

14:06.143 --> 14:08.312
( WAVES GENTLY ROLL )

14:19.490 --> 14:20.491
( CHILDREN SHRIEKING )

14:25.454 --> 14:27.122
( BIRD SINGS )

14:31.377 --> 14:33.629
( BABY CRIES )

15:04.868 --> 15:06.453
( BABY LAUGHS )

15:21.093 --> 15:22.177
( METALLIC CLANKING )

15:25.222 --> 15:27.224
Guys, you're all gonna think I'm crazy

15:27.433 --> 15:29.143
but it feels like a metal man is coming.

15:29.893 --> 15:32.438
( GROANS )

15:44.491 --> 15:45.576
( GRUNTS )

15:47.703 --> 15:48.704
( GROANS )

15:49.788 --> 15:51.081
( ALL SCREAM )

16:04.595 --> 16:05.596
( APPA ROARS )

16:15.606 --> 16:17.191
AZULA: I thought
I'd find you here.

16:17.274 --> 16:21.195
Those summers we spent
here seem so long ago.

16:21.278 --> 16:23.614
So much has changed.

16:23.697 --> 16:25.032
Come down to the beach with me.

16:25.491 --> 16:28.076
Come on, this place is depressing.

16:40.005 --> 16:41.215
Hey...

16:41.423 --> 16:43.091
Where's your new boyfriend?

16:46.428 --> 16:48.430
Are you cold?

16:48.847 --> 16:51.308
I'm freezing.

16:51.642 --> 16:53.393
I'll make a fire.

16:53.477 --> 16:56.855
ZUKO: There's plenty of
stuff to burn in there.

16:56.980 --> 16:57.981
( GROWLS )

17:00.817 --> 17:02.569
This is crazy.

17:02.653 --> 17:04.905
How can we beat a guy who blows
things up with his mind?

17:04.988 --> 17:05.989
We can.

17:06.156 --> 17:07.199
Jump on Appa.

17:07.282 --> 17:08.325
I'll try to distract him.

17:23.590 --> 17:26.051
( PANTING )

17:28.345 --> 17:31.223
( HEAVY FOOTSTEPS THUD )

17:39.189 --> 17:41.942
( HEAVY FOOTSTEPS CONTINUE )

18:23.191 --> 18:24.735
( APPA GROWLS )

18:24.943 --> 18:27.487
( SIGHS ) I'm OK.

18:27.696 --> 18:28.697
Well, that was random.

18:28.864 --> 18:30.449
I don't think so.

18:30.532 --> 18:33.243
I get the feeling he knows who we are.

18:33.452 --> 18:35.912
( FIRE CRACKLING )

18:38.415 --> 18:40.334
TY LEE: What are you doing?

18:40.417 --> 18:42.044
What does it look like I'm doing.

18:42.252 --> 18:44.588
But it's a painting of your family.

18:44.671 --> 18:45.672
You think I care?

18:45.756 --> 18:47.049
I think you do.

18:47.174 --> 18:50.844
You don't know me, so why don't
you just mind your own business?

18:51.261 --> 18:52.888
Ah, I know you.

18:53.096 --> 18:54.473
No, you don't.

18:54.556 --> 18:56.224
You're stuck in your little Ty Lee world

18:56.308 --> 18:57.934
where everything's great all the time.

18:58.018 --> 18:59.978
Zuko, leave her alone.

19:00.062 --> 19:01.813
( MOCKING ) I'm so pretty, look at me.

19:01.897 --> 19:03.815
I can walk on my hands, whoo!

19:07.444 --> 19:08.779
Circus freak.

19:08.987 --> 19:10.739
( LAUGHS )

19:10.947 --> 19:12.783
Yes, I'm a circus freak.

19:12.991 --> 19:14.826
Go ahead and laugh all you want.

19:14.993 --> 19:17.037
You wanna know why I joined the circus?

19:17.245 --> 19:18.830
Here we go.

19:18.914 --> 19:21.416
TY LEE: Do you have any idea
what my home life was like

19:21.500 --> 19:22.834
growing up with six sisters

19:22.918 --> 19:25.128
who look exactly like me?

19:25.253 --> 19:27.756
It was like,
I didn't even have my own name.

19:27.964 --> 19:29.466
I joined the circus because

19:29.675 --> 19:31.885
I was scared of spending
the rest of my life

19:32.094 --> 19:33.929
as part of a matched set.

19:34.137 --> 19:35.472
At least, I'm different now.

19:35.681 --> 19:38.475
Circus freak is a compliment.

19:38.684 --> 19:41.895
Guess that explains why you
need 10 boyfriends, too.

19:42.104 --> 19:43.647
I'm sorry, what?

19:43.855 --> 19:45.607
Attention issues?

19:45.816 --> 19:47.567
You couldn't get enough
attention when you were a kid

19:47.651 --> 19:50.112
so you're trying to make up for it now.

19:50.320 --> 19:53.323
Well, what's your excuse, Mai?

19:53.532 --> 19:55.534
You were an only child for 15 years.

19:55.617 --> 19:57.369
But even with all that attention

19:57.536 --> 20:00.455
your aura is this dingy, pasty, gray...

20:00.580 --> 20:02.916
I don't believe in auras.

20:02.999 --> 20:05.293
Yeah, you don't believe in anything.

20:05.377 --> 20:09.214
Oh, well, I'm sorry I can't be as
high-strung and crazy as the rest of you.

20:09.297 --> 20:11.216
ZUKO: I'm sorry, too.

20:11.299 --> 20:13.635
I wish you would be
high-strung and crazy for once

20:13.719 --> 20:16.138
instead of keeping all your
feelings bottled up inside.

20:16.221 --> 20:17.889
She just called your aura dingy.

20:18.140 --> 20:19.141
Are you gonna take that?

20:19.391 --> 20:21.309
What do you want from me?

20:21.393 --> 20:24.479
You want a teary confession
about how hard my childhood was?

20:24.771 --> 20:26.398
Well, it wasn't.

20:26.565 --> 20:29.192
I was a rich only child
who got anything I wanted

20:29.401 --> 20:31.403
as long as I behaved...

20:31.862 --> 20:34.156
...And sat still

20:34.364 --> 20:36.783
and didn't speak unless spoken to.

20:36.992 --> 20:39.661
My mother said I had
to keep out of trouble.

20:39.870 --> 20:41.997
We had my dad's political
career to think about.

20:42.205 --> 20:44.124
AZULA: Well, that's it, then.

20:44.332 --> 20:46.793
You had a controlling mother
who had certain expectations

20:46.877 --> 20:48.795
and if you strayed from them
you were shut down.

20:49.129 --> 20:51.339
That's why you're afraid
to care about anything

20:51.548 --> 20:52.549
and why you can't express yourself.

20:52.758 --> 20:54.676
You want me to express myself?

20:54.885 --> 20:55.886
Leave me alone!

20:58.430 --> 21:00.682
I like it when you express yourself.

21:00.891 --> 21:01.975
Don't touch me.

21:02.184 --> 21:04.394
I'm still mad at you.

21:04.603 --> 21:07.689
My life hasn't been that easy,
either, Mai.

21:07.773 --> 21:10.317
Whatever. That doesn't excuse the way
you've been acting.

21:10.650 --> 21:12.235
TY LEE: Calm down, you guys.

21:12.444 --> 21:14.654
This much negative energy
is bad for your skin.

21:14.738 --> 21:16.239
You'll totally break out.

21:16.323 --> 21:17.741
ZUKO: Bad skin?

21:17.824 --> 21:19.659
Normal teenagers worry about bad skin.

21:19.785 --> 21:21.661
I don't have that luxury.

21:21.745 --> 21:24.915
My father decided to teach me
a permanent lesson on my face.

21:25.582 --> 21:27.667
Sorry, Zuko, I...

21:27.751 --> 21:30.629
For so long, I thought
that if my dad accepted me, I'd be happy.

21:30.712 --> 21:31.713
I'm back home, now.

21:31.797 --> 21:33.089
My dad talks to me.

21:33.173 --> 21:35.383
Huh, he even thinks I'm a hero.

21:35.467 --> 21:36.802
Everything should be perfect, right?

21:36.885 --> 21:39.179
I should be happy now, but I'm not.

21:39.262 --> 21:41.723
I'm angrier than ever
and I don't know why.

21:42.182 --> 21:44.142
There's a simple question
you need to answer then.

21:44.601 --> 21:46.019
Who are you angry at?

21:46.102 --> 21:48.522
No one, I'm just angry.

21:48.605 --> 21:51.191
Yeah, who are you angry at, Zuko?

21:51.650 --> 21:54.194
Everyone... I don't know.

21:54.277 --> 21:55.320
Is it Dad?

21:55.403 --> 21:56.696
No, no.

21:56.905 --> 21:57.948
- Your uncle?
- Me?

21:58.156 --> 21:59.991
No, no... No, no.

22:00.200 --> 22:01.284
Then who?

22:01.493 --> 22:02.536
Who are you angry at?

22:02.619 --> 22:03.703
Answer the question, Zuko.

22:03.787 --> 22:05.121
TY LEE: Talk to us.

22:05.205 --> 22:06.206
MAI: Come on, answer the question.

22:06.289 --> 22:07.457
AZULA: Come on, answer it.

22:08.208 --> 22:10.460
ZUKO: I'm angry at myself.

22:15.465 --> 22:16.633
AZULA: Why?

22:16.842 --> 22:19.219
Because I'm confused.

22:19.302 --> 22:21.012
Because I'm not sure I know the difference

22:21.096 --> 22:22.556
between right and wrong anymore.

22:22.764 --> 22:24.015
You're pathetic.

22:24.474 --> 22:27.227
MAI: I know one thing I care about...

22:27.435 --> 22:28.854
I care about you.

22:30.897 --> 22:32.482
( LONE HAND CLAP )

22:32.566 --> 22:36.152
Well, those were wonderful
performances, everyone.

22:36.361 --> 22:39.239
I guess you wouldn't understand,
would you, Azula

22:39.447 --> 22:41.032
because you're just so perfect.

22:41.241 --> 22:43.326
Well, yes, I guess you're right.

22:43.410 --> 22:45.620
I don't have sob stories like all of you.

22:45.829 --> 22:48.582
I could sit here and complain how our mom
liked Zuko more than me

22:48.665 --> 22:51.418
but I don't really care.

22:51.626 --> 22:52.961
My own mother...

22:53.169 --> 22:54.754
Thought I was a monster.

22:58.008 --> 23:02.012
She was right, of course,
but it still hurt.

23:02.220 --> 23:04.472
TY LEE: What Lo and Li said came true.

23:04.681 --> 23:06.433
The beach did help us
learn about ourselves.

23:06.641 --> 23:08.727
I feel all smoothed.

23:08.810 --> 23:10.604
I'll always remember this.

23:10.687 --> 23:13.815
You know what would make
this trip really memorable?

23:17.736 --> 23:20.155
We've got some bad news, Chan.

23:20.363 --> 23:21.489
Party's over.

23:23.241 --> 23:24.743
( SCREAMING )

23:24.826 --> 23:25.827
( GRUNTS )

23:35.795 --> 23:36.796
( CRYING LOUDLY )

23:46.556 --> 23:48.099
( ♪... )

23:48.183 --> 23:50.101
( MEN VOCALIZING RHYTHMICALLY )
